#. Diagram label
msgid "Phases 2–4 BPA + requirements"
msgstr ""

#: processes/process/crdm-requirements.bpmn:108
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Process_BeanClose: end the bean in a state that says why — complete and archive it, scrap it with its reasons and archive it, or record the blocker and hand it back. The one place resolve and archive are drawn (bean m8gz, owner 2026-10-24); placed straight before the end so the engine's resolve sees nothing left but the archive step."
msgstr ""

#: processes/process/crdm-requirements.bpmn:98
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Process_BeanOpen: check before you create, find out whose the bean is, and claim it — or leave it alone when it is someone else's. The one place a claim is drawn (bean m8gz, owner 2026-10-24); the gateway after this reads which end it reached."
msgstr ""

#: processes/process/crdm-requirements.bpmn:102
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Reads which end Process_BeanOpen reached. `claimed`: the bean is in progress and this process works it. `not yours`: a sibling session or a human holds it, nothing was written to it, and this process stops here rather than work a bean it does not own (bean-coordination)."
msgstr ""

#: processes/process/crdm-requirements.bpmn:61
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Recognise the request as a platform capability change rather than content work, from crdm-detect's signals. Never call it \"CRDM\" to the person. Mid-content-work, ask whether to pause for requirements now or record a bean for later — do not switch on your own."
msgstr ""

#: processes/process/crdm-requirements.bpmn:105
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Someone else holds the bean; this run stops without touching it."
msgstr ""

#: processes/process/crdm-requirements.bpmn:85
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "The approved requirements become work-plan items, the BA signs off, and the branch is announced on the issue. The announcement is on the single edge into delivery, so the three loops back into implementation do not re-announce."
msgstr ""

#: processes/process/crdm-requirements.bpmn:55
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "The BA describes the capability gap in their own words. They do not need to know it is called CRDM."
msgstr ""

#: processes/process/crdm-requirements.bpmn:29
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "The one activity in this diagram that is not a subprocess call: states the capability gap in its own words and, per its own documentation, does not need to know any of what follows is called CRDM. The six phases translate the need into that vocabulary, not the other way round."
msgstr ""

#: processes/process/crdm-requirements.bpmn:93
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "The stakeholders sign off, the BA confirms every criterion is met, and only then does the agent close the issue. Never the other way round: an agent must never assume completion."
msgstr ""

#: processes/process/crdm-requirements.bpmn:115
#. Diagram label
msgid "yes"
msgstr ""
